WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.040
Westworld Season 3 Episode 4 starts with William.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.540
He’s mad with “grief” and “guilt”
, because last season, William killed his

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:14.640
daughter Emily, because he thought she was
a host . He’s also haunted by the suicide

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:20.580
of his wife Juliet – he wakes up in a bath
like she died in a bath, and sees water raining

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.070
from a chandelier, just like when she died.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:30.490
This chandelier has one red sphere, and five
black ones – just like Dolores had one red

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:33.980
pearl, and five black pearls, including her
own.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:40.379
William’s haunted by a vision of Emily,
who says William destroyed their family – including

00:00:40.379 --> 00:00:45.850
her uncle Logan, and her grandfather James
Delos . William didn’t directly kill these

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:52.129
guys, but his domineering, self-destructive
hidden nature did lead to his family’s downfall

00:00:52.129 --> 00:00:56.010
– its “collapse” like a “dark star”
.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:01:00.429
William says he knows what’s real , and
he’s in control . But he doesn’t want

00:01:00.429 --> 00:01:04.379
to take responsibility for the terrible impact
he’s had on people.

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:09.689
So it’s a paradox, like the problem of evil
– either he is in control, and he’s a

00:01:09.689 --> 00:01:15.369
terrible person, or he’s not in control,
and he’s a helpless machine . Emily shows

00:01:15.369 --> 00:01:21.210
him his profile from last season – the data
from the Forge which records his crimes, and

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:26.899
shows the “code” he follows like a host
. Last season, William wanted to destroy the

00:01:26.899 --> 00:01:31.909
Forge , cause he wanted to escape “judgement”
, and he wanted to prevent himself being made

00:01:31.909 --> 00:01:38.520
into an immortal host in a loop, like James
Delos . So in a sense, William wanted to destroy

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:43.360
himself . He shoots at mirrors, which represents
self-destruction.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:49.929
He considers literal death, cause it’s the
only way he feels he can prove he has control.

00:01:49.929 --> 00:01:55.750
But even that is taken from him .
William gets a visit from the host Charlotte.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:02:01.240
She warns William that Serac is about to take
over the Delos company, and to use the Forge

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.240
data – [that’s “the project in Sector
16”].

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:06.350
So William agrees to help Charlotte – but
it’s all a trick.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:10.350
Charlotte shaves William, just like Dolores
shaved William in Season 1.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:14.690
It’s a symbol of control – letting someone
put a knife to your throat shows that you

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:17.420
know they’d never dare to hurt you.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:21.920
But really, Charlotte is in control here,
and is manipulating William.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.540
Cause Charlotte is not really Charlotte.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:30.100
It’s revealed that this Charlotte, and this
Martin, and this Musashi are all copies of

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:35.160
Dolores . These pearls Dolores brought from
Westworld aren’t the minds of other hosts,

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.740
they’re just copies of Dolores’ mind put
into all these bodies.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:44.520
And Charlotte isn’t really getting William’s
help, she’s having him committed to a mental

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:50.510
hospital, as revenge for his years of abuse
of Dolores . Charlotte also seems to inject

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:54.120
something into William, or maybe take a blood
sample?

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.900
Maybe to track William, or drugs to make him
crazy or something.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:03.510
With William committed, Charlotte takes over
his shares in Delos, so that should help Dolores

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:06.980
take control of the company back from Serac
.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:12.450
So William ends up in the mental hospital
– the Man in Black is now all in white.

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:18.230
He’s got a glove on his right hand because
last season it was injured fighting Dolores.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:24.020
William is now trapped much like James Delos
was trapped – the exact situation he hoped

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:25.020
to avoid.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:31.630
A vision of Dolores says that William is a
prisoner of his own sins . William’s only

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:37.700
problem in this whole story has been his own
paranoia, obsession, and self-destruction.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:43.170
So the only way he can have freedom is to
change, to find his humanity, face his trauma,

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.100
be a half-decent person.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.590
That was the idea of the Door quest last season.

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:54.090
Ford told him to make it out of the park , Emily
told him to come home to his family . But

00:03:54.090 --> 00:04:00.320
William failed, and continues to fail – trapped
in a prison of his own sins.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:05.070
He doesn’t even know if he’s real . Last
season, we saw a flash-forward to the far

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:10.820
future where a copy of William is stuck in
a loop – a fidelity test to see if William

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:16.840
can ever escape his cycle of violence . Maybe
all these scenes are just part of that loop

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:20.620
, and William’s already been replaced with
a host.

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:24.890
Maybe his punishment is to never know if he’s
real.

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:29.200
So can William ever change his nature, and
escape?

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:35.390
Or is this infinite endless prison the end
to William’s story?

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:41.130
We see Bernard in a simulation, being created
by Dolores . It's not clear if this happened

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:45.681
in the Cradle in Westworld, or at Arnold’s
house in the real world, or if this might

00:04:45.681 --> 00:04:48.890
even be the original Bernard being made years
ago.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:54.680
But the point is that Bernard and Arnold are
important to Dolores – he’s a father figure,

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:59.160
who believed that the hosts could grow into
real people , and that’s part of why Dolores

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:03.060
remade Bernard, even though she knows he’ll
try to stop her.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:07.310
Bernard has a flashback of Arnold’s son
Charlie, which reminds us that this Bernard

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:09.410
is part Arnold.

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:12.220
Bernard and Stubbs were both created in Westworld.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:15.680
Now, they get to hang out in the real world
for the first time.

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:20.640
So naturally, they sink some beers in southern
California – and everything’s pretty familiar,

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:25.580
except now in the future, they’ve got reusable
landing rockets like SpaceX.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:30.741
Stubbs mentions a shoulder injury , because
the actor Luke Hemsworth hurt his arm, which

00:05:30.741 --> 00:05:36.120
forced a rewrite of the fight scene in Episode
2 . Bernard thinks that Dolores has killed

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:40.000
Liam Dempsey and replaced him with a host,
and wants to stop her.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:44.230
So Bernard makes a little clicker button that
can freeze hosts, like what Serac used to

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:45.590
freeze Maeve.

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:50.750
The robot lads dress up and prepare to play
a new role.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:54.780
Dolores and Caleb go shopping – there’s
some technology that digitally shows what

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:59.280
clothes look like on you – this kinda stuff
has been developed in the real world.

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:04.050
Caleb feels uncomfortable buying fancy clothes
– cause he’s a working class guy, this

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:10.430
isn’t his style . But Dolores says that
style is just a marker of class and tribe,

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:12.530
like animals with plumage.

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:18.270
Like hosts, humans dress up to play roles,
and once you see that, and break free of your

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:22.600
role, and you can use that code to manipulate
others . [As in “dress code”!]

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:24.550
Dolores wants Liam Dempsey’s money.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:29.020
So she gets the Martin host to get Liam’s
financial authorisation key.

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:33.419
Liam is one of the richest tech bros in the
world , but he lets Martin handle all his

00:06:33.419 --> 00:06:39.010
financial and security stuff, so he can spend
his time partying . It seems like freedom,

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:41.620
but really Martin’s in control.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:45.790
So this rich man is no more free than a host.

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:50.060
Dolores also steals the blood of Liam’s
money guy, Michael, so that Caleb can use

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:53.770
the security markers in his blood to impersonate
Michael.

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:57.910
Caleb is nervous, his palms are sweaty , but
he successfully plays the “role” of a

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:02.530
rich asshole , and steals all Liam’s money
– showing how status and class are just

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:06.780
as artificial and coded as the roles that
hosts follow.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:10.419
Maeve chats with Serac in a fancy Singapore
bar.

00:07:10.419 --> 00:07:13.910
And Serac explains why he wants to control
the world.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:19.660
When Serac was a kid, he saw Paris destroyed
. A Westworld trailer mentions a “thermonuclear

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:24.120
incident” in Paris in 2025 so it must be
that.

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:29.300
Serac and his brother look weirdly similar
to young Ford and his brother, who we saw

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:30.630
as hosts.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:33.570
Is it possible that Serac and Ford were brothers?

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:39.860
Or do all children look that in 2025, frolicking
in fields in formal dress?

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:45.050
Either way, the point is that young Serac
witnessed a terrible preventable tragedy,

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:49.690
so he wants to control everything to prevent
disasters from happening again – to stop

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:54.770
humanity from destroying itself . It’s a
pretty good reason to wanna rule the world.

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:59.960
But it also raises questions about freedom
– should we let ourselves be controlled

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:00.960
to save lives?

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:05.290
[Corona yo, stay at home] Serac controls the
world with data technology on the computer

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:10.390
Rehoboam and the Incite company, but his data
is not yet complete.

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:13.090
He wants Westworld’s data, from the Forge.

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:18.730
Cause the Forge data is the most “complete”
“map of the human mind” . In Season 1,

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:22.600
the whole idea of the Westworld park is that
it gives people the freedom to reveal their

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:23.840
true selves.

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:29.360
Like, William, outside the park, acts like
a “family man” and a “good guy” , but

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:34.649
inside the park, he reveals his true dark
self . That’s why the Westworld data would

00:08:34.649 --> 00:08:40.309
be valuable to Serac – with data on the
real true identities and choices of the human

00:08:40.309 --> 00:08:46.339
mind, he could better control people, like
Caleb, and everyone else in the world.

00:08:46.339 --> 00:08:51.459
Apparently the key to unlock this data is
in Dolores , so Serac wants Maeve to capture

00:08:51.459 --> 00:08:57.129
Dolores for him – now that we know there
are at least four Dolores’ – is the key

00:08:57.129 --> 00:09:00.940
in all of them, or just one, or split between
them, or what?

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:06.600
But in return, Serac says he’ll upload Maeve
into the Sublime, the digital paradise for

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:11.410
hosts, so she can be with her daughter in
robot heaven forever . We were told that the

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:16.750
Sublime was sealed away and inaccessible,
but Serac claims he can get Maeve in anyway

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:23.230
. And if she doesn’t comply, he says he’ll
trap her in a digital hell forever . So Serac

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:29.140
plays the role of a devil, tempting Maeve
into conflict, promising paradise – but

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:33.420
maybe he can’t be trusted, and his promises
are empty.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:37.629
Serac takes Maeve to Arnold’s house, and
says this is where the “divergence” started

00:09:37.629 --> 00:09:39.990
which threatens Serac’s plans.

00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:44.629
All these circular images this season seem
to be from the computer Rehoboam identifying

00:09:44.629 --> 00:09:47.360
people who are going against Serac’s plan.

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:51.709
He thinks the Doloreses are the big threat
to his plans , but Bernard also came from

00:09:51.709 --> 00:09:54.720
here – maybe he’s the big threat to Serac.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:10:00.190
We see that Dolores printed five host bodies
here – she made herself a Dolores body,

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:03.999
and Bernard, and Martinlores, and Musashilores.

00:10:03.999 --> 00:10:09.269
And she printed the new Charlotte – unless
she just reused the Charlotte body she came

00:10:09.269 --> 00:10:10.269
in.

00:10:10.269 --> 00:10:15.999
If so, there could be a mysterious unknown
fifth host for Dolores’ fifth pearl out

00:10:15.999 --> 00:10:17.339
there somewhere.

00:10:17.339 --> 00:10:22.410
Serac has this guy Jiang, an identity broker,
who helped Dolores set up her fake identity

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:28.519
as Lara . Serac interrogates Jiang, and shows
him images of his family suffering.

00:10:28.519 --> 00:10:33.470
Serac says he’s not gonna hurt Jiang’s
family, this isn’t a threat, it’s a true

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:39.629
simulation of what the world will do to Jiang’s
family if Serac fails and Dolores wins , which

00:10:39.629 --> 00:10:44.309
suggests that the world would really be better
off under Serac’s control.

00:10:44.309 --> 00:10:49.869
But then Serac murders Jiang, so Serac is
still villainous – he kills people in his

00:10:49.869 --> 00:10:52.569
quest to save people.

00:10:52.569 --> 00:10:57.399
Maeve follows Jiang’s information to a woman
called The Mortician, who provided blood for

00:10:57.399 --> 00:10:59.050
Dolores’ fake identity.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:04.869
The Mortician treats human bodies like objects
to be chopped apart and sold, just like how

00:11:04.869 --> 00:11:07.410
host bodies are treated in Westworld.

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:11.269
Maeve hacks the Mortician’s device to stop
her calling for help.

00:11:11.269 --> 00:11:15.019
Maeve learned some super l33t hackerman skills
in Westworld.

00:11:15.019 --> 00:11:20.459
The Mortician refers Maeve to the Yakuza,
so Maeve finds their base at Itaidoshin Distillery.

00:11:20.459 --> 00:11:26.389
Itai Doshin is a Buddhist concept about unity,
literally meaning many bodies, with one mind

00:11:26.389 --> 00:11:32.129
. This refers to how Dolores has copied her
one mind into many bodies.

00:11:32.129 --> 00:11:35.990
The Yakuza have cyberpunk guns that aim automatically.

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:39.769
So Maeve hacks them so the Yakuza all shoot
each other.

00:11:39.769 --> 00:11:44.759
Maeve learns that the Yakuza’s new leader,
called Sato, is actually the host Musashi,

00:11:44.759 --> 00:11:47.959
who Maeve met in Shogunworld last season.

00:11:47.959 --> 00:11:51.080
Musashi complains that Maeve left him to die
in the park.

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:55.980
Maeve says it was Musashi’s choice to stay,
but Musashi says the choice wasn’t real,

00:11:55.980 --> 00:12:00.329
because Musashi didn’t know that he was
a robot in a theme park . This is similar

00:12:00.329 --> 00:12:05.540
to how William says his choice to kill Emily
wasn’t a real choice, because he didn’t

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:07.319
know that Emily was human.

00:12:07.319 --> 00:12:10.059
But this Musashi isn’t really Musashi.

00:12:10.059 --> 00:12:14.139
He, and this Martin, and this Charlotte, are
actually all copies of Dolores.

00:12:14.139 --> 00:12:19.579
Because the only person Dolores trusts to
be her ally is herself . It seems that Dolores

00:12:19.579 --> 00:12:24.420
isn’t taking over the world for all hosts,
she’s just filling it with copies of herself

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:30.569
, like Agent Smith in The Matrix, she’s
spreading and replicating like a virus.

00:12:30.569 --> 00:12:35.339
The Yakuza base is full of this white goo,
that’s used to make hosts.

00:12:35.339 --> 00:12:41.160
Maybe Dolores is making a heap of bodies to
copy herself into, an army of herself to fill

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:42.160
the world.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:46.769
But she also talks about building a world
for Maeve’s daughter , so maybe she’ll

00:12:46.769 --> 00:12:51.679
take the real world for herself, and build
a virtual world for other hosts, and leave

00:12:51.679 --> 00:12:54.749
no world at all for humanity.

00:12:54.749 --> 00:13:00.269
Musashi kills Maeve, and she bleeds out into
the white host goo, just like this host bleeding

00:13:00.269 --> 00:13:02.749
into milk in Season 1.

00:13:02.749 --> 00:13:09.130
Milk is connected to motherhood, birth, creation
and growth, while blood is connected to death.

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:15.410
The Season 1 intro had this milky white stuff,
and Season 3 intro has this red stuff, playing

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:18.269
with these concepts of birth and death.

00:13:18.269 --> 00:13:22.959
And if you mixed em together, you’d probably
get something like Caleb’s strawberry shake.

00:13:22.959 --> 00:13:27.559
Musashilores goes to take Maeve’s pearl,
so that Serac can’t keep using Maeve, but

00:13:27.559 --> 00:13:32.279
then he leaves it behind cause they run out
of time, or cause Maeve is being tracked or

00:13:32.279 --> 00:13:33.279
something?

00:13:33.279 --> 00:13:37.850
It’s weird to not take the pearl – maybe
Musashi-lores believes that even if Maeve’s

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:42.850
fighting against them, she has a role to play,
just like Bernard .

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:47.589
Liam and Roderick and Penny go to a fancy
sex party for rich people, like in Eyes Wide

00:13:47.589 --> 00:13:51.999
Shut , while a classical rendition of Wicked
Games by the Weeknd plays.

00:13:51.999 --> 00:13:57.589
High class sex workers are displayed on pedestals,
and auctioned off for cash.

00:13:57.589 --> 00:14:02.049
Roderick says that “All sex is commerce”
, which is like what Maeve says in Season

00:14:02.049 --> 00:14:06.970
1 , in her brothel . Liam and Roderick’s
dynamic is much like William and Logan in

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:07.970
the park.

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:13.089
The point is that in both Westworld and the
real world, people are objectified, sex is

00:14:13.089 --> 00:14:18.769
a commodity, and the world is a playground
to gratify the rich . Dolores says that the

00:14:18.769 --> 00:14:24.299
real world is no different to Westworld .
Roderick gives Liam a fancy new drug called

00:14:24.299 --> 00:14:30.060
Genre, that “Sends you straight to the silent
era” . The next Westworld episode is called

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:35.319
Genre, and Liam still has that drug – so
maybe next episode will be a drug trip to

00:14:35.319 --> 00:14:40.000
the “silent era” – like that one episode
of Watchmen, where a drug trip takes a character

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.019
to the black-and-white era.

00:14:42.019 --> 00:14:45.480
You might wanna watch our Watchmen videos,
they’re pretty good.

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:50.059
Bernard crashes the party and tries to freeze
Liam with his button, but it doesn’t work,

00:14:50.059 --> 00:14:54.489
because Liam’s still a human, not replaced
with a host . If Dolores wanted to replace

00:14:54.489 --> 00:14:58.860
Liam with a host, she probably could have
done it when he was alone with Martin earlier.

00:14:58.860 --> 00:15:02.779
She must want Liam alive as a human for some
reason .

00:15:02.779 --> 00:15:05.100
Dolores intercepts, and fights with Stubbs.

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:09.029
Which is sad, cause Stubbs doesn’t want
to fight, he’s just been programmed to by

00:15:09.029 --> 00:15:15.129
Bernard . Three seasons in, and the hosts
are still forced to fight each other in coded

00:15:15.129 --> 00:15:16.420
conflicts.

00:15:16.420 --> 00:15:21.259
Penny and Roderick are surprised to see Dolores
kung-fu fighting robots at a sex party – cause

00:15:21.259 --> 00:15:23.310
they thought she was dead.

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:27.579
Dolores taps the side of her head, cause she
once said to Roderick that’s the nucleus

00:15:27.579 --> 00:15:34.459
accumbens, which evolved to make humans believe
in God . Now Dolores is like God – undying,

00:15:34.459 --> 00:15:40.480
omnipresent, and unstoppable – Dolores once
said that “The real gods are coming” , so

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:43.339
Roderick best start believing.

00:15:43.339 --> 00:15:48.470
Martin captures Bernard, and Dolores captures
Liam, and as all the storylines sync up, it’s

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:54.089
simultaneously revealed that Charlotte and
Martin and Musashi are all copies of Dolores.

00:15:54.089 --> 00:15:59.579
The reason why this is interesting is that
as we learned last episode, these copies aren’t

00:15:59.579 --> 00:16:04.559
identical clones – they’re more like Dolores’
children, who grow and change and make their

00:16:04.559 --> 00:16:05.959
own decisions.

00:16:05.959 --> 00:16:09.639
So they might not all follow Dolores’ plans.

00:16:09.639 --> 00:16:15.699
This episode is called “The Mother of Exiles”,
which refers to a poem on the Statue of Liberty.

00:16:15.699 --> 00:16:21.029
It frames the statue as a symbol of hope,
a powerful maternal figure who’ll welcome

00:16:21.029 --> 00:16:26.970
and protect the downtrodden . So is Dolores
this Mother of Exiles – will she protect

00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:30.559
the downtrodden, like Caleb, and her host
children?

00:16:30.559 --> 00:16:33.509
Or is she just taking the world for herself?

00:16:33.509 --> 00:16:37.369
Is Maeve the saviour, at least for hosts like
her daughter?

00:16:37.369 --> 00:16:42.309
Or Might Bernard be the real hope, a more
compassionate compromising person who doesn’t

00:16:42.309 --> 00:16:44.359
fucken murder people all the time?

00:16:44.359 --> 00:16:47.819
Will Serac save humanity, despite his brutality?

00:16:47.819 --> 00:16:51.870
Or will one of the Dolores copies find new
possibilities?

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:55.459
Or are D&amp;D the saviours we need after all?

00:16:55.459 --> 00:17:01.470
Westworld presents lots of different perspectives
on freedom hope and control.

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:04.459
So Itai Doshin is a Buddhist concept.

00:17:04.459 --> 00:17:08.459
Buddhism has been practiced for thousands
of years, and a lot of it is about how to

00:17:08.459 --> 00:17:15.360
deal with suffering – so in stressful uncertain
times, Buddhist texts can be really helpful,

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:19.089
regardless of whether you consider yourself
religious or spiritual.

00:17:19.089 --> 00:17:23.009
If you’ve never read any Buddhist stuff,
you might like to start with the Dhammapada

00:17:23.009 --> 00:17:27.850
– it’s simple and short and wise and practical
and an absolute banger, and you can get it

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:32.210
on audiobook for free right now by signing
up for a trial with Audible.

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:36.549
Members get an audiobook each month, and if
